    "q-149600": {
      "dom_id": "step-q149600",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{50}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{100}4({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij})\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{50}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{100}{a}_{ij}=40,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{50}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{100}{b}_{ij}=60.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The sum and constant multiple rules for double summations state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{ij}, \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}k{a}_{ij} & =k{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying these rules to the given sum, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{50}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{100}4({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}) & =4{\\sum }_{i=1}^{50}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{100}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}) \\\\  & =4{\\sum }_{i=1}^{50}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{100}{a}_{ij}+4{\\sum }_{i=1}^{50}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{100}{b}_{ij} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 40+4\\cdot 60 \\\\  & =160+240 \\\\  & =400.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
