    "q-149738": {
      "dom_id": "step-q149738",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{13}({a}_{i}-2)({b}_{j}-5)\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{a}_{i}=35,\\,{\\sum }_{j=1}^{13}{b}_{j}=70.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The product rule for double summations states that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{i}{b}_{j}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{a}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, using the product rule for double summations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{13}({a}_{i}-2)({b}_{j}-5) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}({a}_{i}-2){\\sum }_{j=1}^{13}({b}_{j}-5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the rules for single summations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}({a}_{i}-2){\\sum }_{j=1}^{13}({b}_{j}-5) & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{a}_{i}-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}2)\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{13}{b}_{j}-{\\sum }_{j=1}^{13}5) \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{a}_{i}-2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}1)\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{13}{b}_{j}-5{\\sum }_{j=1}^{13}1) \\\\  & =(35-2\\cdot 10)\\cdot (70-5\\cdot 13) \\\\  & =(35-20)\\cdot (70-65) \\\\  & =(15)\\cdot (5) \\\\  & =75.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
